  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures a high-energy set by the Mountain Goats at The Salt Shed in Chicago, Illinois, on Friday, June 30, 2023 [1][2]. As the support act for The Hold Steady, the band was limited to a sixty-minute performance, which they utilized to deliver a densely packed hour of music [1]. The audio is a matrix mix combining soundboard and audience microphones, providing a balanced perspective on the live event [1]. The setlist features fourteen songs, drawing from various albums including *All Eternals Deck*, *In League with Dragons*, and *Bleed Out* [1]. Notable tracks include “Liza Forever Minnelli,” “Younger,” and “Birth of Serpents” [1]. The performance also includes “An Antidote for Strychnine,” a song with only twelve archived performances in the collection [1][2]. Later in the set, the band plays “Abandoned Flesh,” “The Diaz Brothers,” and “Dance Music” [1]. The uploader notes that the band provided spoken introductions for the final song, “No Children,” and mentioned skipping a song [1]. This is the 373rd archived show for the performer, following a previous recording at the Mercury Ballroom on June 29, 2023 [2]. The file is the only available recording of this specific date, with documented lineage from the tapper [1].",
